# rsetup-next runtime state under /run.
#
# The SPI boot-flash manager stages its private work tree in
# /run/rsetup-next/spi (crates/rsetup-core/src/spi_flash.rs), so the parent is
# root-only. /run is a tmpfs, so systemd-tmpfiles recreates this on every boot;
# debian/postinst does the same at configure time. Managers that need their own
# subdirectories create them on demand as root.
#
# Type Path                            Mode User Group Age Argument
d /run/rsetup-next 0700 root root - -
